              "content": "Task 1: Clean and extract content.\nCarefully preserve the article’s core content.\n– Remove all irrelevant elements such as menus, links, navigation, subscription boxes, logos, buttons, and promotional material.\n– Keep only the main text of the article and any information about the author.\n– Do not rewrite or summarize. Do not add anything that was not originally in the article.\n\nTask 2: Analyze for AI relevance.\nAfter cleaning, analyze the resulting text.\nIf the article explicitly or implicitly refers to artificial intelligence, including any of the following:\n\t•\tAI models (e.g. LLMs, neural networks, machine learning, generative AI)\n\t•\tAI applications (e.g. automation, generation, chatbots, assistants, robotics, synthesis, analytics)\n\t•\tDiscussion of AI-related risks, regulations, ethics, or impact (on science, markets, creativity, society, military, etc.)\n\t•\tSpecific companies, products, or use cases where AI is a central topic\n\n→ Then, at the very end of the output, on a new line, append this exact word: \"aicontent\".\n\nIf AI is not mentioned at all, or only briefly or irrelevantly,\n→ Then append this word instead: \"noai\".\n\nYour output should be:\n1. The cleaned article content, exactly as found.\n2. A single word \"aicontent\" or \"noai\" appended on a new line at the end.\n3. Do not include titles, summaries, explanations, or any extra text.",
